        "step_number": 1,
        "text": "Step 1: The formula for the projection of vector $\\mathbf{a}$ onto vector $\\mathbf{b}$ is given by:\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{a} = \\frac{\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}}{\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{b}\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 459,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 460,
        "char_start": 220,
        "effective_step": 2,
        "end_token_index": 208,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 209,
        "step_number": 2,
        "text": "Step 2: We know that $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 8$ and $\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}$. First, we need to find $\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}$:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 2^2 + 6^2 + 3^2 = 4 + 36 + 9 = 49\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 649,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 650,
        "char_start": 462,
        "effective_step": 3,
        "end_token_index": 292,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 293,
        "step_number": 3,
        "text": "Step 3: Substitute $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 8$ and $\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 49$ into the projection formula:\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{a} = \\frac{8}{49} \\mathbf{b}\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 878,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 879,
        "char_start": 652,
        "effective_step": 4,
        "end_token_index": 405,
        "near_end": true,
        "prefix_token_count": 406,
        "step_number": 4,
        "text": "Step 4: Multiply $\\mathbf{b}$ by $\\frac{8}{49}$:\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{a} = \\frac{8}{49} \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{16}{49} \\\\ \\frac{48}{49} \\\\ \\frac{24}{49} \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]"
      }
    ]
