  "raw_text": "Step 1: The formula for the projection of vector $\\mathbf{a}$ onto vector $\\mathbf{b}$ is given by:\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{a} = \\frac{\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}}{\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{b}\n\\]\n\nStep 2: We know that $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 8$ and $\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}$. First, we need to find $\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}$:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 2^2 + 6^2 + 3^2 = 4 + 36 + 9 = 49\n\\]\n\nStep 3: Substitute $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 8$ and $\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 49$ into the projection formula:\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{a} = \\frac{8}{49} \\mathbf{b}\n\\]\n\nStep 4: Multiply $\\mathbf{b}$ by $\\frac{8}{49}$:\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{a} = \\frac{8}{49} \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{16}{49} \\\\ \\frac{48}{49} \\\\ \\frac{24}{49} \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{16}{49} \\\\ \\frac{48}{49} \\\\ \\frac{24}{49} \\end{pmatrix}}<|im_end|>",
